97b59382" "question-a41968c0-9f0e-5476-a397-0981a383aad9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142601 :question/problem "What is the reciprocal of $9?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $9$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n9= \\dfrac{9} 1\n$$\n\nTo find the reciprocal of a fraction, we switch the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}9}{\\color{red}1} \\quad\\rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{\\color{red}1}{\\color{blue}9}\n$$\n\nSo the reciprocal of $9$ is $\\dfrac{1}{9}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142840 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-46e3f780-030d-57e1-a5a9-d79b60c0b975" "question-466ad742-32a5-51ef-8790-152f9b4cba3e" "question-9db77aa7-416e-5aa0-a065-40719b047014" "question-a0c12612-4312-5182-90fc-74e72ef9cb63" "question-b0c97c18-5089-5b56-8eda-7c5d4d9b07d7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142602 :question/problem "What is the reciprocal of $2\\,\\dfrac{2}{5}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given mixed number to an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\dfrac{2}{5} = \\dfrac{(2\\times 5)+2}{5}=\\dfrac{12}{5}\n$$\n\nTo find the reciprocal of a fraction, we switch the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}12}{\\color{red}5} \\quad\\rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{blue}12}\n$$\n\nSo the reciprocal of $2\\,\\dfrac{2}{5}$ is $\\dfrac{5}{12}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143250 :question/problem "The reciprocal of $\\frac{1}{2}$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the reciprocal of a fraction, we switch the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\to \\,\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}=2\n$$\n\nSo, the reciprocal of $\\frac{1}{2}$ is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186140496 :answer-field/correct "answer-4d08df97-318d-5347-a931-7134bfc49f6b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d08df97-318d-534